{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205","id":5209104168,"node_id":"PR_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABNnyfKA","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205","diff_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1205","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1205/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/statuses/7d4db26a2ce75e9942badaca954bb8e8f821c75c","number":1205,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add guarded campaign curation and canonical publication operators","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The ten-worker unmatched-ingredient campaign needs guarded source application and canonical publication for an explicitly reviewed multi-owner plan. These operators bind frozen source cases, published proposals, acceptance, producer bytes and complete owner inventories before writing, then preserve recoverable receipts and native publication lineage.\n\nDepends on #1158 at `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`; the base remains that dependency branch. Campaign ingredient edits and release products belong in a separate dependent PR after final scientific and plan acceptance. No maintained campaign owner has been applied, and no merge is requested.\n\nCurrent code head: `7d4db26a2ce75e9942badaca954bb8e8f821c75c`. Independent final-head re-review is running; **application approval remains pending**. This ordinary five-file commit fixes the two #1256 residuals [filed before correction](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1256#issuecomment-6721304487): hidden staged-index changes and a commit during the last live publisher source-proof replay.\n\nIndependent initial replays now confirm those two original failures are refused. A further source index-coherence defect remains: a real staged-entry change between cached enumeration and blob verification can escape the final check. [W08-7D4DB26-SRC-001 was filed before correction](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1256#issuecomment-6721505891). The exact7d4 head remains unapproved; its full local QC/test run has not started. A bounded correction and another exact-head review are required.\n\n- Source application checks both literal NUL-delimited working and cached paths, refusing unrelated staged changes even when working bytes are restored. Changed staged owner entries must match a real installed accepted endpoint; future or different blobs, modes and premature deletions are refused.\n- Publication checks accepted baseline HEAD after complete prepare, dry-run output preflight and the entire live recheck, including actual source-proof replay. Legitimate later historical verification remains supported; ordinary uncommitted derived synchronization remains allowed.\n- #1251 preserves inherited collision families while refusing new pairs. #1252 permits bounded rejected-record maintenance and genuine UNMAPPED-to-REJECTED retirement while preserving identity, path and history guards.\n- #741's explicit demotion requires a separately reviewed exact relocation tuple, genuine published origins and no prior owner chain on either path. MAPPED-to-AMBIGUOUS demotion removes grounding, requires zero generated subject/registry rows and removes every old slot through native position maps. It does not decide Angustmycin A/C identity.\n- #1255 preserves authentic Unicode and other literal Git filenames. Origin, collision, relocation, held-position, exclusive-output and actual-native-producer guards remain in force.\n\nAddresses #1174, #1194, #1195, #1197, #1198, #1200, #1214, #1251, #1252, #1255 and #1256, plus the bounded #741 workflow prerequisite. Earlier findings, failed probes and superseded reviews remain preserved. Existing archives under `reports/unmatched_campaign_operators_1174_20261108/independent-review/` and `issue1214/` retain their identities. The [earlier review receipt](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205#issuecomment-6718353021) applies only to its stated head.\n\nValidation and independent-review checkpoints:\n\n- Current source tests: all354 passed, including53 new cases. The same private combined command had157 publisher setup failures from omitted historical fixture dependencies; its complete failure log is retained. A separate correctly configured run passed164 publisher/integration cases against both final operators, including20 real pinned-Claw cases, with zero skips. These are separate runs, not a claimed single518-case run. Ruff, Black and Mypy passed on the corrected files.\n- The source's previous301 tests are an exact byte prefix; the publisher's previous68 test-function ASTs/assertions are unchanged. All new changes add regression coverage. Historical #1255 test harness changes require earlier refusal rather than weakened checks. No tests removed or skipped; no gate, workflow, threshold or pin changed.\n- Worker08's exact21061 review passed458 tests yet found both residual defects; its verdict remains `needs_curation`. Its technical, skeptical and assembly reports are preserved. Worker08 has actually accepted the separate exact7d4db26 review and will replay the residual probes before deeper tests.\n- Historical16c `just qc` and full `just test` passed:5654 passed,116 existing skips,31 warnings; all nine then-existing real-native cases ran.21061QC passed, but its full local suite was deliberately interrupted after145 partial passes when the defects were confirmed. Neither historical checkpoint substitutes for final-head QC/full tests or CI.\n- Real native integration uses isolated Claw `76c1ebeea3fc7f80bf1abe044688f298f390cfac` and immutable eac469f1 with27 historical receipts. CI may skip optional external-root integration when those roots are unavailable; local native execution is separately evidenced. Rule B4's missing default ontology path is disclosed rather than claimed as complete label verification.\n\nRoot verified75 source and132 publisher packet members before ordinary commit/push. Author source manifest `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/source-index1256-fix-v1/MANIFEST.json`: `c609c872e7a66a69d33640554653379c7d75a47d33c4caefa03e11fae83ea64c`. Publisher `publisher-late-head1256-fix-v2/portable/MANIFEST.json`: `7646e523c9f7bc0c790250767091c568b1f81fb69eff3a90d2f815e10592c5fa`. Commit receipt: `preflight/residual1256-commit-v1/receipt.json` under the same campaign root.\n\nA bounded archive proposal is under separate independent review; final code review and validation evidence will be added with explicit scope. This implementation PR grants no scientific identity, role, owner or supported-export approval.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T06:01:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T12:30:52Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5dac36d33b3933dfeff250c952aac513084c7db3","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CultureBotAI:curate/all-unmatched-source-integration-20261107","ref":"curate/all-unmatched-source-integration-20261107","repo":{"id":1175495445,"node_id":"R_kgDORhCjFQ","name":"MediaIngredientMech","full_name":"CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","owner":{"login":"CultureBotAI","id":233210009,"node_id":"O_kgDODeaAmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233210009?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CultureBotAI/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Curated Media Ingredient Ontology Mappings with LLM-Assisted Workflows","homepage":"https://culturebotai.github.io/MediaIngredientMech/","language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics